<%# Global impersonation bar — a slim amber strip across the very top of every
    page, mobile and desktop, for as long as a superadmin is impersonating.

    It replaces the old copies that lived inside the mobile hamburger panel and
    at the bottom of the desktop sidebar: both were easy to browse past for a
    long time without any reminder of whose account you were standing in.

    Three things, one type size: the word, the name, and Stop on the right.

    Every other piece of chrome pinned to the top of the viewport carries
    `app-top-chrome` and is pushed down by --impersonation-bar-h; see the
    `body.impersonating` rules in app/assets/tailwind/application.css. Keep the
    height here (h-8) and that variable in sync. %>
<div id="impersonation-bar" class="fixed inset-x-0 top-0 z-[70] bg-amber-500 text-white">
  <div class="flex h-8 items-center justify-between gap-3 px-3 sm:px-5">
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2 min-w-0 text-xs font-bold">
      <span class="uppercase tracking-wider flex-shrink-0">Impersonating</span>
      <span class="truncate"><%= Current.user.person&.name || Current.user.email_address %></span>
    </div>
    <%= render "shared/button", text: "Stop", variant: "outline", size: "xs",
          path: stop_impersonating_user_path, method: :post, classes: "flex-shrink-0" %>
  </div>
</div>
